{'symbol': 'PCG', 'date': '2021-03-09 12:00:00', 'title': "PG&E SURPASSES CALIFORNIA'S 2020 RENEWABLE ENERGY GOAL; ELECTRICITY DELIVERED TO CUSTOMERS IS MORE THAN 88% GREENHOUSE GAS-FREE AND AMONG THE CLEANEST IN THE NATION", 'text': "SAN FRANCISCO--(BUSINESS WIRE)--PACIFIC GAS AND ELECTRIC COMPANY (PG&E) EXCEEDED CALIFORNIA'S RENEWABLES PORTFOLIO STANDARD (RPS) GOAL REQUIRING ENERGY PROVIDERS TO DELIVER 33% RENEWABLE ENERGY BY THE END OF 2020. PG&E ESTIMATES THAT IT DELIVERED OVER 35% FROM SPECIFIED ELIGIBLE-RENEWABLE RESOURCES TO ITS CUSTOMERS LAST YEAR, ACCORDING TO ITS RECENT FORM 10-K. OVERALL, MORE THAN 88% OF THE ELECTRICITY PG&E DELIVERED TO ITS CUSTOMERS LAST YEAR CAME FROM GREENHOUSE GAS (GHG)-FREE RESO"}